About WPP Production

We are WPP Production - the unified global production company that brings together all of WPP's content producers, studios and craft experts into one connected organisation. We combine world-class human craft with next generation technology to originate, design, and deliver multi-channel content systems at scale. Built for borderless collaboration and powered by deep craft expertise, we are the production engine designed for today's always on, AI driven marketing world.

About WPP

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. We unite&nbsp;cutting-edge media intelligence and data solutions, world-class creativity, next-generation production, transformative enterprise solutions and expert strategic counsel&nbsp;in a single company -&nbsp;powered by exceptional talent and our agentic marketing platform, WPP Open,&nbsp;to help our clients navigate change, capture opportunity and deliver transformational growth. For more information, visit&nbsp; WPP.com .

A Hybrid working model

We believe the best work happens when we're together, fostering creativity, collaboration, and connection. That's why we’ve adopted a hybrid approach, with teams in the office around four days a week. If you require accommodations or flexibility, please discuss this with the hiring team during the interview process.

What does a Production Coordinator do at WPP Production? &nbsp;
As our Studio Coordinator, you’ll keep the studio running smoothly by owning the admin, trackers and reporting that let our creative and production teams focus on making great content. You’ll be the organized, proactive link between briefs, budgets, shoots and suppliers across our markets and our Singapore and Hyderabad hubs.

Reporting&nbsp;lines and&nbsp;key stakeholders: &nbsp;

This role reports to the  Studio Lead.&nbsp;You will work closely with the internal studio team, finance and clients.&nbsp;

Responsibilities:&nbsp;

• Admin: POs, invoices, budgets, contracts, talent releases, and supplier set-up

• Order: own the production tracker, keep drives and the asset library tidy, maintain templates and checklists

• Production support: log briefs, schedule shoots and crew, coordinate samples between markets and our Singapore and Hyderabad hubs

• Reporting: weekly status and monthly volume reports by division and brand

Who we're looking for:

• 1 to 2 years in production coordination, studio admin or operations, ideally in content production.&nbsp;

• Open to fresh graduates with relevant internship experience in content production

• Highly organized and detail-minded; strong with Excel/Sheets and project tools

• Proactive communicator, comfortable working across countries and time zones

• Beauty, FMCG or social content experience is a plus

